By the equation (\ref{eq:dnew}), the bit length of the new vector generated by the unimodular matrix transformation \textbf{UMTrans1} (resp. \textbf{UMTrans2}) is less that $\min\{\underline{\#}(\mathbf{c}+\mathbf{d},\mathbf{c}-\mathbf{d}), \#\mathbf{c}-1\}$. Therefore, the \textbf{while} loop in step \ref{hvec:stepwhile2}  will terminate after at most $4$ iterations  and thus the time complexity is $O(M(n))$. Overall, the total time complexity is 
\begin{align*}
    T(n)=2T\left(\frac{n}{2}\right)+O(M(n))=\left(2^2 T\left(\frac{n}{2^2}\right)+O\left(2\cdot M\left(
    \frac{n}{2}\right)\right)\right)+O(M(n))=O\left(\sum_{i=0}^{\log n}2^i M\left(\frac{n}{2^i}\right)\right).
\end{align*}
Since $M\left(\frac{n}{2^i}\right)\le \frac{1}{2^i}M\left(n\right)$ for $i=0,\cdots,\log n$, 
\begin{align*}
T(n)=O\left(\sum_{i=0}^{\log n}2^i M\left(\frac{n}{2^i}\right)\right)=O\left(M(n)\sum_{i=0}^{\log n}1\right)=O(M(n)\log n).
