\section{Introduction}
\label{sec:introduction}

\IEEEPARstart{U}{nmanned} aerial vehicles (UAVs), also known as drones, have been widely used in fire detection, geological hazard monitoring, and dangerous behavior monitoring~\cite{ruvzic2021application} for their agility, compactness, and cost-efficiency. To reduce the dependency of UAVs on human labor and skills, UAV nests are widely used to minimize manual operations, allowing the UAVs to perform autonomous monitoring. UAV nests also offer functionalities such as safe parking, charging, data transmission, routine maintenance, repairs, and communication relays~\cite{knitter2024survey}. However, automatic UAV landing is a major challenge in the application of UAV nests. In this work, we propose a landing deviation warning system for UAV landing.\par
%In practical applications, UAVs are generally parked in nests, which function as safe parking, power charging, data collection, daily maintenance, repair, and communication relay. Usually, global positioning system (GPS) and Quick Response (QR) Code are combined to correct the flight of the UAVs to achieve landing. However, landing is still the most dangerous stage during the use of UAVs. One of the reasons is that existing autopilot systems highly depend on GPS, which may lose signal in a congested area and is poor at estimating the altitude above the ground~\cite{NAKAMURA201711664}. Furthermore, landing methods based on the Global Positioning System (GPS) are susceptible to interference from geomagnetic storm activity. In urban areas with dense skyscrapers or mountainous terrain, GPS accuracy may be compromised due to obstruction issues.~\cite{wing2005consumer} Additionally, achieving precision landing in such scenarios requires a substantial number of sensors, posing significant challenges to the system.
%早期用于无人机着陆定位的系统主要是基于跟踪雷达或全球定位系统以及地面标志物。大部分的自动驾驶定位系统高度依赖GPS，而GPS在估算地面高度方面表现不佳。此外，基于GPS定位的着陆方法容易受到地磁风暴活动的干扰。在高楼密集的城市或山区，GPS的精度也可能会因障碍物问题而受到影响。随着计算机视觉技术的发展,基于视觉的定位降落在无人机中得到了广泛应用。与易受环境因素影响且获取信息单一的基于GPS的定位降落方法相比，基于视觉的定位方法是实现稳健自主降落的经济高效且可靠的解决方案。视觉方法可以分为两类：1）模型驱动方法；2）数据驱动方法。模型驱动方法依赖于手工设计的特征提取和图像处理算法，例如边缘检测、形状匹配、纹理分析等。开发者需要对图像特征有深刻理解，并编写特定算法来识别和处理这些特征。较为刚性，特征提取和处理方法通常是固定的，对环境变化和噪声的鲁棒性较低，需要大量的调整和优化才能适应不同应用场景。数据驱动方法依赖于深度学习模型，尤其是卷积神经网络（CNN），通过大量数据进行训练自动提取图像特征。这些模型能够学习到复杂的特征表示，而无需人为干预。

