%。然而，传统视觉方法通常依赖于手工设计的特征提取算法和使用预定义的分类器和回归器来执行任务。由于室外环境的不确定性，使用基于传统视觉系统的方法在获得高精度方面存在困难。这是因为基于传统视觉的着陆算法在以下几个方面面临着挑战：

The challenge of vision-based UAV landing lies in providing quick and accurate warnings of deviations. Segmentation methods can accurately obtain the target shape, however, due to the lack of detection frame constraints, they may generate artifacts that mislead localization (\autoref{show}(b)) and the model's slow speed makes it challenging to meet real-time application requirements. The target detection methods \cite{zhang2022dino} can locate the target. Nevertheless, the vertical detection frame cannot effectively capture the shape and orientation of the target when it rotates substantially (\autoref{show}(c)). %\textcolor{red}{ As illustrated in \autoref{show}(a), the multitask model, which integrates detection and segmentation, is utilized to accurately locate the landing area.}%In contrast, our multitask model can combine the advantages of detection and segmentation to accurately locate the landing area, as shown in\autoref{show}(a).



%\textcolor{red}{We propose AeroLite-MDNet for UAV landing deviation, a lightweight multitask model that integrates both detection and segmentation in a multi-scale framework.} 
To address the issues, we propose a lightweight and multitask learning model, AeroLite-MDNet. We reduce the model parameters by keeping the core architecture and multi-scale fusion unchanged while reducing the depth of the three convolutional layers (C3) module, limiting the parameter size to millions to achieve real-time inference. Data enhancement techniques such as random flipping and image blending are used to improve the generalization to the changes in the environment. Meanwhile, multi-task joint learning is employed to capture multi-level information, where the detection branch provides the location and category of the target, and the segmentation branch provides the shape and region of the target (\autoref{show}(a)).

The main contributions of this paper can be summarized as follows:

\begin{enumerate}

  %  \item For UAV landing deviation warning in complex backgrounds, we propose a lightweight, multi-scale detection and segmentation multitask model, AeroLite-MDNet. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first multitask model that combines detection and segmentation for the task of UAV landing.

  %  \item \textcolor{red}{To address the dynamic changes in target scale during landing, we designed a differentiated attention multi-scale fusion module. This module incorporates spatial and channel attention based on the contributions of different levels of target features. It adaptively enhances hierarchical multi-scale features while suppressing background, thereby improving the model's performance. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed model, with only 7.12 million parameters, achieves real-time inference speeds of 104.2 FPS on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 GPU while maintaining high-precision warning accuracy at 98.6\%}.

  %  % \item To evaluate the performance of the UAV landing deviation detection system, we propose AWD as a new metric. This metric provides a practical measure of the delay during the system's warning process, which is critical for ensuring timely and reliable landing decisions.
  %  \item \textcolor{red}{To meet the deployment requirements of embedded edge devices, we further optimized the model architecture and adopted ONNX acceleration strategies, achieving real-time inference capabilities on the NVIDIA Jetson TX2 development board. Experimental results demonstrate that AeroLite-MDNet maintains equivalent warning accuracy while operating stably at 7.3 FPS on the Jetson TX2 platform, validating the feasibility of high energy-efficient deployment of the model on UAV onboard edge computing devices.}
  % \item \textcolor{red}{We collected a UAV landing dataset named UAVLandData from UAV videos, which comprises 9,142 high-quality images extracted from over 13 hours of landing videos, covering 24 diverse scenarios with varying weather and lighting. Each image is annotated with bounding boxes and pixel-level segmentation labels, ensuring robust model training and evaluation across real-world conditions.}

\item For UAV landing deviation warning in real-world environments, we propose AeroLite-MDNet, a lightweight multi-scale detection-segmentation multitask model, representing the first UAV landing deviation detection framework integrating dual-task detection and segmentation.


\item We collect UAVLandData, a landing dataset containing 9,142 images from 13-hour videos across 24 scenarios with diverse weather/lighting conditions, annotated with bounding boxes and pixel-level segmentation masks. 


\item  The model achieves 104.2 frames per second (FPS) on RTX 3070 with 7.12M parameters and 98.6\% warning accuracy. Optimized with ONNX acceleration, the model achieves 7.3 FPS on Jetson TX2, demonstrating efficient edge deployment capability.
