%\textcolor{red}{In this work, we discussed image segmentation-related approaches that combine image classification networks with feature fusion modules. Farabet et al.~\cite{farabet2012learning} proposed an image pyramid approach that uses a multiscale convolutional network trained from raw pixels to extract dense feature vectors. These feature vectors encode regions of multiple sizes centered on each pixel and merge feature maps from all scales. However, this model is less suitable for larger DCNNs due to limited GPU memory. UNet~\cite{ronneberger2015u} and SegNet~\cite{badrinarayanan2017segnet} employ a U-shaped encoding-decoding structure with skip connections, and experimental results have shown the effectiveness of such models on various semantic segmentation benchmarks. The aforementioned methods have limitations, such as the need for substantial computational resources or insufficient accuracy, which do not meet the requirements for UAV landing.}


