\section{Discussion}
The proposed method performs well in monitoring UAV landings in various environments. However, the current system mainly relies on RGB cameras, additional spotlights are required for illumination at night, increasing system complexity and energy consumption. Future research could consider integrating multiple types of sensors, such as infrared cameras, LiDAR, or millimeter-wave radar, to enhance perception in various environments and improve overall robustness and adaptability. Moreover, the current approach focuses on monitoring, with limited integration into the UAV control system. Future work may explore integration, such as jointly optimizing perception and control. This would enable more efficient coordination and response during the landing process, further improving landing accuracy and stability.
