\section{Conclusion}

In conclusion, we propose a novel and highly interpretable method that combines high-dimensional Hawkes processes with Graph Neural Networks for modeling opinion propagation on social media. By introducing the VISTA dataset, which includes multi-level comment structures, sentiment annotations, and interactions between trending topics, we provide valuable research data for future studies on opinion dynamics. Our method effectively captures the temporal evolution, structural changes, and sentiment diffusion patterns in discussions. In the future, we plan to apply more advanced methods on this dataset to further explore the underlying mechanisms of opinion dynamics.




