%     \textsc{Temporal Reachability Edge Deletion} can be solved in time $O(n\Lambda \phi^2\phi+3^{6\phi^2}(\phi^2)^{18\phi^2}(3\phi^3+\phi^3))=O(n\Lambda \phi^3+3^{6\phi^2}\phi^{36\phi^2})$, where $\Lambda$ is the lifetime of the input temporal graph, $n$ the number of vertices, and $\phi$ the TIM width.
% \end{corollary}
\section{Future work and conclusions}\label{sec:conclusion}

In this work, we define the new parameter TIM width, a generalisation of VIM width, and give meta-algorithms with respect to both parameters. These meta-algorithms can be applied to large families of problems which include \textsc{Temporal Hamiltonian Path}, $\Delta$-\textsc{Temporal Matching}, and \textsc{Temporal Reachability Edge Deletion}. While the meta-algorithm for VIM-width can also be applied to \textsc{Temporal Firefighter}, we find that this problem remains NP-hard on temporal graphs of bounded TIM width and $\geq$-connected-VIM width, resolving an open problem posed by Christodoulou et al.~\cite{christodoulou_making_2024}.
