\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Experimental Settings}

\textbf{Datasets and Evaluation Metrics} We evaluate our model on seven benchmark datasets: 
(1) \textbf{General Question Answering}: NQ \cite{Natural_Questions}, TriviaQA \cite{JoshiTriviaQA2017}, and PopQA \cite{mallen2023trustlanguagemodelsinvestigating}. 
(2) \textbf{Multi-Hop Question Answering}: HotpotQA \cite{yang2018hotpotqa}, 2WikiMultiHopQA \cite{xanh2020_2wikimultihop}, Musique \cite{trivedi2021musique}, and Bamboogle \cite{press-etal-2023-measuring}. 
HotpotQA is in-domain benchmark since a portion of its training sets is used for training while others serve as out-of-domain benchmarks to assess our model’s generalization capabilities.
For evaluation metric, we utilize Exact Match (EM) following \cite{yu2024rankragunifyingcontextranking}.

\textbf{Baselines} We compare our method against the following baselines: 
(1) \textbf{Naive Generation}: Generating answers directly without retrieval. 
(2) \textbf{Standard RAG}: Traditional retrieval-augmented generation systems. 
(3)\textbf{RAG-CoT Methods}: Integration of retrieval-augmented generation with chain-of-thought prompts, such as IRCoT \cite{IRCoT} and Search-o1 \cite{Search-o1}. 
(4) \textbf{RAG-RL Methods}: Utilizing reinforcement learning to allow the model to autonomously perform retrieval during inference, such as Search-R1~\cite{Search-R1} and R1-Searcher~\cite{R1-Searcher}.

\textbf{Implementation Details} We utilize Qwen-2.5-7B-Instruct as the backbone models for our training and all baseline models. 
For retrieval, we use the English Wikipedia provided by KILT \cite{KILT} in 2019 as retrieval corpus, segmented into 100-word passages with appended titles, totaling 29 million passages. 
We employ BGE-large-en-v1.5 \cite{bge_m3} as the text retriever and set the number of retrieved passages to 3 across all retrieval-based methods to ensure fair comparison. 
The maximum number of retrieval is set to 4. 
More details on the experimental settings are provided in Appendix \ref{Implementation_Details}.

