\begin{lemma}[\cite{askotch}]\label{rls-projection}
Let $\A\in\R^{n\times n}$ be psd and $\lambda'>0$. Let $\{p_i\}_{i=1}^n$ be $O(1)$-approximate $\lambda'$-ridge leverage score sampling probabilities. Let $\S \in \R^{O(d_{\lambda'}(\A)\log^3 n) \times n}$ be a random sub-sampling matrix, drawn from probability distribution $\{p_i\}_{i=1}^n$. Consider the random projection matrix $\P=\A^{1/2}\S^\top(\S\A\S^\top)^\dagger\S\A^{1/2}$. Then $\E[\P]$ satisfies 
\begin{align}
\E[\P] ~\succeq~ \frac12 \A \left(\A + \lambda'\I\right)^{-1}.
\end{align}
