In Table \ref{tab:ablation}, while continual pretraining (CPT) and supervised fine-tuning (SFT) can improve the performance separately, the combination of CPT and SFT consistently yields the best performance. This indicates that these methods may complement each other. A detailed analysis of this phenomenon in section \ref{fig: case_study} shows that CPT may be good at providing domain knowledge, while SFT enhances task generation style.

