\begin{lemma}
 For all $i>1$ and  $m\geq m_i$, there exists a unique sequence $S_{i,m}$ of binary delimiters that is  well-ordered for $(i,m)$. Furthermore, the length of $S_{i,m}$ is $m^{i-1}$.
