Here, $\mathcal L_r$ represents the set of links whose LLEs are necessary to fulfill a type $r$ request. A type $r$ request is successfully served if the measurement operation applied on LLEs of the links in $\mathcal L_r$ is successful. Note that LLEs used in measurement operations are always discarded irrespective of the outcome of measurement operations. 

Since we consider a two-sided matching system, we will typically consider requests on the \emph{right-hand side} and the links on the \emph{left-hand side}. See Figure~\ref{Fig:sm_qs}. 
