\subsection{Quantum Switch dynamics}
We now describe the dynamics of the quantum switch discussed in Section \ref{subsec:topology}.  Here we consider a discrete-time model.

\subsubsection{Order of events.} Over one time-slot,
the following sequence of events occurs. First, new LLEs are generated between each link and the switch.
Next, the number of requests of each type for service is decided. Then, an LLE schedule is selected. 
A number of these scheduled requests will fail.
These requests will not be removed, but the LLE will have decoherence and thus will be removed.
%This results in a schedule which attempts to connected the LLEs associated with those requests. This step involves processing each type of requests by utilizing the available LLEs at each link.
Next, toward the end of the time slot, new arrivals for requests occur.
Finally, at the end of the time slot, a number of leftover LLEs will decohere.

