Since $\bar{Q}_r(s)>0$ for $s\in [0,t]$ and $\bar{Q}^c_r(s)$ convergences uniformly to $\bar{Q}_r(s)>0$, there exists a value of $c'$ for which $\bar{Q}^c_r(s)$ is strictly bounded away from zero for all $c\geq c'$. Since queues are non-zero,
