\]
satisfies $\phi_{m_1,m_2,m_3,m_4}(x)$ on $\Mscr_\BLP$. For each $m\geq 2$ we define
\[
\phi_{m,1,1,1}(x)\equiv \phi_{O,m}(x),
\]
where $\phi_{O,m}(x)$ is the internal reference to $O^\Ical$ defined in 
Claim 7. Now suppose that $i>1$
is the maximum index such that $m_i>1$. We have two cases. Suppose that $m_i$ is odd. Then we let
$n_i= m_i-1$, $n_j= m_j$ for all $j\neq i$, and define
\begin{align*}
\phi_{m_1,m_2,m_3,m_4}(x)\equiv \exists y \exists^6 z
& \Big( 
\phi_{n_1,n_2, n_3, n_4}(y)
\wedge  \\
&  \phi_{E_i}(z) 
\wedge y = z^{(1,2,3,4,5,5)}
