    \{0\},\{1\}, \emptyset)
    \sim_p (
    \{1\},\{0\}, \emptyset)$, proves the statement. Suppose that $p\geq 3$.
    Without loss of generality we can assume that $\omega= ( \{0\}, \{m\}, \ZZ_p \setminus \{0,m\})$ for some $m\in \ZZ_p$. We find witnesses $\overline{\omega_{y_i}}$,
