     Finally, using again that $\overline{\omega_y}\sim_\Dcal 
    \overline{\omega_x}^{(1,2)}$, we obtain again that $\overline{x}$ belongs to $D_1$, as we wanted to prove. \par
    Now, in order to see that $\overline{\omega_p}$
    satisfies $\phi_{1,p}(x)$ on $\overline{\Cscr}$, just consider $\overline{\omega_y}$ as a witness for $y$, where $\omega_y$ is the tuple
    $(\{0 \}, \ZZ_p \setminus \{0\}, \emptyset ) \in \Cscr_p$, and apply the previous claim. 
