\subsection{Mask Comparison}
\label{sec:mask_compare}
To quantitatively confirm the quality of our masks (i.e., edited regions), we randomly sampled 100 entries and asked 3 human evaluators to score the masks generated by different methods on a scale of 1(worse) to 5(best). These methods include the bounding boxes generated by GPT-4o, the masks produced by DiffEdit\cite{couairon2022diffedit}, and the masks generated by our pipeline. As shown in Table.~\ref{tab:supp_mask_comparison}, our average mask quality score is 4.01, which is significantly higher than the other two methods. In addition to quantitative experiment, some visual results are presented in Figure.~\ref{fig:supp_mask_vis}.

\begin{table}[h]
    \caption{\textbf{Human ratings of mask generated by different methods.}}
    \centering
    \begin{tabular}{c|ccc}
    \toprule
                & GPT-4o & DiffEdit & Ours \\ \hline
    Human rating & 2.66   & 1.45     & \textbf{4.01} \\ \bottomrule
    \end{tabular}
    \label{tab:supp_mask_comparison}
\end{table}

